# `DCS tmux; ... ST` carries a sequence meant for the outer terminal, with inner
# escapes doubled. Un-doubling yields a real SGR, so the text that follows is
# styled -- the payload is applied, not printed.
size: 16x3
description: tmux passthrough applies its un-doubled payload

--- input
\ePtmux;\e\e[1m\stBOLD

--- expect-cell
row=0 col=0 text=B bold=true
